  hamiltonian_paths=1

Conclusion
  The same carry coordinate toggles even/odd parity and decides the n=14 apex obstruction.  Non-multiple rows are already discharged by t=1/14; the required multiple-of-14 branch is the congruence k_i == r_i mod 14.  Every minimal apex lift over AP/V*, and every one/two extra-toggle neighbourhood screened here, is strictly above the floor in exact group minima, with no near-floor or below-floor rows detected.
  This does not prove LRC(14), but it moves the carry-conservativity seam: a new primitive floor lift would need a larger globally coherent carry cocycle or an owner/Cprime route, not merely the first parity/apex bridge.
